course: dictionary
lesson: 6065
title: Merge: joining to become one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To merge means to join together so that two or more things become one. Rivers do it, roads do it, and so do companies and schools. «In the disc, dust stuck into pebbles, pebbles into rocks, and these crashed and merged into planets.» Here merged means the rocks joined together to become one planet.
explain: You can often find the meaning of merge from the words around it. When traffic merges, two lanes join into one. When a computer merges cells, it puts them together so they become one bigger cell. In both cases, the things were separate before and become one afterwards.
explain: Merge often goes with small words. You can merge into something, like a small road merging into a motorway, or merge with something, like a stream merging with a river. Notice the pattern: the things always end up together.
fact: To merge means to join together to become one.
fact: «Merged» is the past tense of merge, and «merging» is the -ing form.
fact: When traffic merges, two lanes join into one.
fact: On a computer, to merge cells means to put them together into one cell.
fact: In maths, merging two groups means adding them together.
fact: «Merge into» and «merge with» are common phrases, as in «the stream merges with the river».
exercise: «In the disc, dust stuck into pebbles, pebbles into rocks, and these crashed and merged into planets.» What does merged mean here? | Split apart and scattered | Stopped moving | *Joined together to become one | Got lighter and floated away
exercise: When traffic merges, what happens? | Every car gets a new lane | Cars stop completely at the side of the road | *Two lanes join into one | Two lanes stop and the cars go backwards
exercise: On a computer, what does it mean to merge cells? | Make each cell a different colour | Delete every cell in the table | *Put the cells together into one cell | Copy each cell onto a new page
test: «When two people change the same part of the code, the changes must be merged; tools like Git help teams combine their work.» What does merged mean in this sentence? | *Joined together into one | Argued about until they stopped | Printed out on paper | Deleted and forgotten
test: Fill in the gap: The two small streams ___ into one wide river. | argue | *merge | shrink | split
exam: In maths, what does merging two groups mean? | Taking one group away from the other | Splitting them into halves | *Adding them together | Counting only the first group
